ation that remains useful in daily work</h1> <p>A process description only helps when employees recognize the real workflow. IBS-Saxony documents for practical handovers and improvements, not just for a folder.</p> <a class="button button-gold" href="/en/contact">Free initial call</a> </div> </section> <section class="section section-soft"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Starting point</span> <h2>Typical gaps in established workflows</h2> <p>In small and medium-sized companies, process knowledge often lives in individual heads, emails and personal routines. This becomes visible when tasks must be handed over, covered or digitalized.</p> </div> <div class="card-grid three"> <article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">01</span><h3>Knowledge held by individuals</h3><p>Cover staff and new employees must reconstruct workflows from conversations, messages and example files.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">02</span><h3>Unclear interfaces</h3><p>Information moves between phone, email, paper and software without a reliable handover point.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">03</span><h3>Documentation without a daily-use test</h3><p>Existing descriptions are too abstract, outdated or omit roles, inputs and outcomes.</p></article> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Approach</span> <h2>From the real task to a usable workflow map</h2> <p>The scope stays deliberately small: one workflow, its inputs and results, and the points where friction occurs today.</p> </div> <div class="step-grid"> <article class="step-card"><span>01</span><h3>Capture the current workflow</h3><p>One responsible person walks through the real task and shows existing documents and systems.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span>02</span><h3>Make handovers visible</h3><p>Roles, triggers, documents, decisions and system changes are organized in clear language.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span>03</span><h3>Prioritize improvement</h3><p>Together, we define which bottleneck should be reduced first and how the benefit can be checked.</p></article> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section section-soft"> <div class="container narrow service-card related-card"> <span class="section-kicker">Subject context</span> <h2>Related application context</h2> <p>For agricultural businesses, the digital agricultural office shows why findable documents and clear data workflows matter. The approach can also help other regional businesses, but is always checked against the actual process.</p> <a class="text-link" href="https://www.landwirtschaft.sachsen.de/digitales-agrarbuero-dokumentenmanagement-69902.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LfULG: digital agricultural office and document management (German)</a> </div> </section> <section class="section section-dark"> <div class="container narrow"> <span class="section-kicker">Boundaries</span> <p>The documentation maps operational workflows. It does not replace legal, tax, occupational-safety or other required professional review.</p> <a class="text-link" href="/en/digital-agricultural-office-saxony">Digital agricultural office in Saxony</a> </div> </section> <section class="section final-cta"> <div class="container"> <span class="section-kicker">Next step</span> <h2>Start with one manageable process</h2> <p>In the free process call, we review which workflow should be documented and relieved first.</p> <a class="button button-gold" href="/en/contact">Free initial call</a> </div> </section>  </main> <footer class="site-footer"> <div class="footer-grid"> <div> <img class="footer-logo" src="/assets/logo-ibs-saxony-white.png" alt="IBS-Saxony"> <p>Process optimization, systems integration and digital tools for companies in Saxony.</p> <details class="footer-legal-note"> <summary><span>Legal notice</span></summary> <p>IBS-Saxony does not provide legal, insolvency, tax, financial or other binding professional advice. Our support is limited to operational workflows, data, organization and implementation; legal, tax, insolvency or financial questions must be reviewed by qualified professionals.</p> </details> </div> <div> <h2>Quick links</h2> <a href="/en/services">Services</a><a href="/en/process-and-documentation-workflows">Workflows</a><a href="/en/references">Work examples</a><a href="/en/about">About</a><a href="/en/contact">Contact</a> </div> <div> <h2>Contact</h2> <a href="mailto:info@ibs-saxony.com">info@ibs-saxony.com</a> <a href="tel:+4915142495353">+49 1514 2495353</a> <p>Ringstraße 12<br>01612 Nünchritz</p> </div> <div> <h2>Legal</h2> <a href="/en/imprint">Imprint</a> <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy</a> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@ibs-saxony" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">YouTube</a> </div> </div> <div class="footer-bottom"> <span>© 2026 IBS-Saxony UG (haftungsbeschränkt). All rights reserved.</span> <button class="footer-consent" type="button" onclick="window.dispatchEvent(new Event('ibs-saxony-reset-consent'))">Change cookie settings</button> </div> </footer>   <?php if ($ibsHasAnalytics): ?>
